From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:52:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fee review: bound the L1 data fee for the maximum SIGNED
 transaction; no all-fee claim

Root review (ROOT-FEE-REVIEW): getL1Fee(serialized UNSIGNED tx) counts no
signature bytes. The bound now uses the deployed Fjord GasPriceOracle
getL1FeeUpperBound(unsignedTxSize). The oracle adds 68 signature bytes and assumes
the worst fastlz case; these assumptions are explicit in activation.mjs.
txSizes() computes the exact unsigned size (113 bytes here) and the maximum signed
size (180; r = s = 2^256-1, yParity 1). The argument is max(unsigned, signedMax-68),
so the oracle-side size always covers the signed transaction, and
assertCoversSigned refuses anything smaller, including unsigned-only accounting.
Verification refuses a wallet-added access list, which would exceed the bound.

The request's feeBound reports the L2 cap, the L1 upper bound, and their sum
labelled totalExcludingOperatorFeeWei: any OP-stack operator fee is neither read
nor bounded. The page's fee row and the README say so. Existing caps are unchanged.

activation 10/10 (256 MiB). Two fee mutants (unsigned-only oracle argument,
unsigned-only size accounting) fail the suite. Nothing was served or signed.
